1
00:00:11,912 --> 00:00:16,440
Excuse me. My name is Richard Stewart.

2
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:17,370
I'm a photographer.

3
00:00:17,370 --> 00:00:19,388
May I take a picture of you and your little boy?

4
00:00:19,388 --> 00:00:20,228
What's it for?

5
00:00:20,228 --> 00:00:20,846
It's for a book.

6
00:00:20,846 --> 00:00:22,326
Richard Stewart, 46 Linden Street,

7
00:00:22,326 --> 00:00:23,510
You're writing a book?

8
00:00:23,510 --> 00:00:25,157
It's a book of pictures.

9
00:00:25,157 --> 00:00:29,682
I call it Family Album, U.S.A.

10
00:00:29,682 --> 00:00:30,447
Oh, that's a nice idea.

11
00:00:30,447 --> 00:00:34,251
Well, it's fine if you take our picture.

12
00:00:34,251 --> 00:00:36,069
I'm Martha Vann.

13
00:00:36,069 --> 00:00:38,336
Thank you. I appreciate your help.

14
00:00:38,336 --> 00:00:40,386
I'm Richard. What's your name?

15
00:00:40,386 --> 00:00:40,602
Gerald.

16
00:00:40,602 --> 00:00:41,934
How old are you, Gerald?

17
00:00:41,934 --> 00:00:42,134
Five.

18
00:00:41,934 --> 00:00:44,669
And where do you live?

19
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:48,397
We live in California.

20
00:00:48,397 --> 00:00:51,625
Well, welcome to New York.

21
00:00:51,625 --> 00:00:59,559
OK, just a second.

22
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:01,186
I'm almost ready here.

23
00:01:01,186 --> 00:01:07,467
Can I help you?

24
00:01:07,467 --> 00:01:07,931
Oh, please.

25
00:01:07,931 --> 00:01:15,336
Hold Gerald's hand, please. Great!

26
00:01:15,336 --> 00:01:20,405
Now point to the buildings.

27
00:01:20,405 --> 00:01:21,352
Terrific!

28
00:01:21,352 --> 00:01:25,511
Give Mommy a kiss, Gerald. Nice!

29
00:01:25,511 --> 00:01:26,861
Thank you, Gerald.

30
00:01:26,861 --> 00:01:28,111
And thank you, Mrs. Vann.

31
00:01:28,111 --> 00:01:30,672
Oh, my pleasure.

32
00:01:30,672 --> 00:01:39,073
We'll be looking for your book.

33
00:01:39,073 --> 00:01:47,719
Thank you. Good-bye. Bye, Gerald.

34
00:01:47,719 --> 00:01:48,743
Thanks again.

35
00:01:48,743 --> 00:01:50,560
Oh, you're welcome.

36
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:52,810
Hey, let me take your picture!

37
00:01:52,810 --> 00:01:53,563
Wonderful. Please.

38
00:01:53,563 --> 00:01:56,700
Are you from New York?

39
00:01:56,700 --> 00:01:58,284
No, I'm from Greece.

40
00:01:58,284 --> 00:01:59,618
I'm an exchange student.

41
00:01:59,618 --> 00:02:02,096
When did you come here?

42
00:02:02,096 --> 00:02:06,274
Three months ago.

43
00:02:06,274 --> 00:02:08,612
Your English is very good.

44
00:02:08,612 --> 00:02:11,030
Thanks.

45
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:13,030
I studied English in school.

46
00:02:13,030 --> 00:02:14,008
Would you like some coffee?

47
00:02:14,008 --> 00:02:14,865
No, thank you.

48
00:02:14,865 --> 00:02:16,208
Tell me about your book.

49
00:02:16,208 --> 00:02:17,486
Oh, it's not finished yet,

50
00:02:17,486 --> 00:02:22,942
but I have some of the pictures.

51
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:26,895
Would you like to see them?

52
00:02:26,895 --> 00:02:28,195
Yes. I'd like that.

53
00:02:28,195 --> 00:02:31,138
Here they are. Family Album, U.S.A.

54
00:02:31,138 --> 00:02:37,832
It's an album of pictures of the United States:

55
00:02:37,832 --> 00:02:50,487
the cities, the special places, and the people.

56
00:02:50,487 --> 00:02:56,240
And these are pictures of people working:

57
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:57,780
steelworkers, bankers, police, street vendors,

58
00:02:57,780 --> 00:03:00,178
ambulance drivers, doctors....

59
00:03:00,178 --> 00:03:04,634
Oh, this is my father. He's a doctor.

60
00:03:04,634 --> 00:03:06,114
This is my mother.

61
00:03:06,114 --> 00:03:07,002
What's her name?

62
00:03:07,002 --> 00:03:07,298
Ellen.

63
00:03:07,298 --> 00:03:11,349
My younger brother, Robbie.

64
00:03:11,349 --> 00:03:13,567
He goes to high school.

65
00:03:13,567 --> 00:03:15,784
This is my sister Susan.

66
00:03:15,784 --> 00:03:18,654
She works for a toy company.

67
00:03:18,654 --> 00:03:21,383
Here's my grandfather. He lives in Florida.

68
00:03:21,383 --> 00:03:23,358
And this is my wife Marilyn.

69
00:03:23,358 --> 00:03:25,072
Oh, she's very pretty.

70
00:03:25,072 --> 00:03:27,079
Thanks. And what about your family?

71
00:03:27,079 --> 00:03:28,457
They are in Thessaloniki.

72
00:03:28,457 --> 00:03:31,822
That's a large city in northern Greece.

73
00:03:31,822 --> 00:03:38,891
But now I'm living in the Bronx.

74
00:03:38,891 --> 00:03:41,089
With a Greek-American family?

75
00:03:41,089 --> 00:03:41,569
No. Hispanic.

76
00:03:41,569 --> 00:03:43,347
Oh no! It's five thirty.

77
00:03:43,347 --> 00:03:45,347
Will you excuse me?

78
00:03:45,347 --> 00:03:46,858
I have to meet my wife.

79
00:03:46,858 --> 00:03:49,525
It was nice meeting you.

80
00:03:49,525 --> 00:03:50,926
It was a pleasure meeting you, too.

81
00:03:50,926 --> 00:03:52,521
Thanks for your help.

82
00:03:52,521 --> 00:03:55,926
And good luck! I've got to go.

83
00:03:55,926 --> 00:03:58,419
By the way, I'm Richard.

84
00:03:58,419 --> 00:03:58,964
What's your name?

85
00:03:58,964 --> 00:03:59,164
Alexandra.

86
00:03:59,146 --> 00:03:59,873
Bye-bye, Alexandra. Thanks.

87
00:03:59,873 --> 00:04:02,873
Bye-bye. Richard! Richard! You left your bag!
